<Base title="Start learning email | howto.email" description="A guided path through DNS, SMTP, message structure, authentication, transport security, deliverability, security, and troubleshooting."><div class="wrap page article"><p class="kicker">LEARNING PATH</p><h1>Learn email end to end</h1><p>Email makes more sense when you learn the pieces in the order a message actually depends on them. This path uses the existing howto.email library rather than making you guess what to read next.</p>
<h2>1. Build the mental model</h2><p>Start with <a href="/learn/how-email-works/">How email works</a>, then <a href="/learn/email-architecture/">email architecture</a> and <a href="/learn/dns-for-email/">DNS for email</a>.</p>
<h2>2. Understand SMTP and routing</h2><p>Read the <a href="/reference/smtp/">SMTP reference</a>, <a href="/learn/email-routing/">email routing</a>, <a href="/reference/mx/">MX records</a>, and <a href="/learn/why-email-is-store-and-forward/">why email is store-and-forward</a>.</p>
<h2>3. Understand the message itself</h2><p>Continue with <a href="/reference/message-format/">message format</a>, <a href="/learn/email-headers/">email headers</a>, <a href="/reference/mime/">MIME</a>, and the <a href="/do/header-analysis-lab/">header analysis lab</a>.</p>
<h2>4. Learn authentication</h2><p>Read <a href="/learn/email-authentication/">email authentication</a>, then study <a href="/reference/spf/">SPF</a>, <a href="/reference/dkim/">DKIM</a>, <a href="/reference/dmarc/">DMARC</a>, and <a href="/reference/dmarc-alignment/">alignment</a>.</p>
<h2>5. Add transport security</h2><p>Learn <a href="/reference/starttls/">STARTTLS</a>, <a href="/reference/mta-sts/">MTA-STS</a>, <a href="/reference/tls-rpt/">TLS-RPT</a>, and <a href="/reference/dane-smtp/">DANE for SMTP</a>.</p>
<h2>6. Understand deliverability and reputation</h2><p>Move into <a href="/learn/deliverability-basics/">deliverability</a>, <a href="/learn/email-reputation-signals/">reputation signals</a>, <a href="/learn/list-hygiene/">list hygiene</a>, and <a href="/reference/bounce-types/">bounce types</a>.</p>
<h2>7. Learn security and operations</h2><p>Read the <a href="/learn/email-security-model/">email security model</a>, <a href="/learn/email-threats/">email threats</a>, <a href="/learn/business-email-compromise/">BEC</a>, and <a href="/learn/mail-flow-logging/">mail-flow logging</a>.</p>
<h2>8. Practice troubleshooting</h2><p>Use the <a href="/troubleshoot/">troubleshooting hub</a>, work through the <a href="/do/dns-email-lab/">DNS lab</a> and <a href="/do/smtp-session-lab/">SMTP session lab</a>, then inspect a real domain with <a href="/tools/domain-check/">Domain Check</a>.</p></div></Base>